Package: patrone-gnome-taskbar
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, gnome-shell (>= 50~), gnome-shell (<< 51~)
Recommends: patrone-settings
Description: Patrone Desktop's taskbar, for its GNOME-based desktop
 A compact taskbar along the bottom of the screen, in place of GNOME's top
 bar, as on Windows 11: the Start menu, where typing searches apps, settings
 and files at once, with "Search the web" for anything else; pinned apps and
 slots for the default web browser, terminal, file manager and mail app;
 running apps; right-click jump lists with recent files and tasks; and the
 system tray, clock and notifications.
 .
 A GNOME Shell extension (patrone-taskbar@patrone-linux), on by default for
 every account, until Patrone's own shell replaces GNOME Shell.
